WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.320
"Fat-Blocking Benefits of Hibiscus Tea"

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:15.240
Hibiscus tea, also known as roselle or
Jamaica, is enjoyed around the world

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.801
hot or cold for its bright red color
and tart cranberry-like flavor.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.561
It's the "zing" in Red Zinger tea.

00:00:22.561 --> 00:00:24.180
I talk about its benefits
in the chapter

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.220
on high blood pressure
in How Not to Die,

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.480
working as well as some leading
antihypertensive medications

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:37.260
in head-to-head tests, or
even beating the drugs out.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.600
Within three hours
of drinking hibiscus tea,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.060
changes in hundreds
of metabolites can be detected

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.940
in the human bloodstream
with creative names

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.140
like hibiscic acid, or
hibiscin, or hibiscitrin.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.200
Alterations in human gene
expression at the 3-hour mark

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.480
after drinking it suggest
a downregulation

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.660
of cholesterol synthesis and
an improvement in metabolism.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.140
But randomized controlled trials
failed to consistently find

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.460
cholesterol-lowering benefits.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.260
An interesting side-effect
popped up, though: weight loss.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.900
In Mexico, hibiscus tea
has been traditionally used

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.200
as a treatment for obesity,
sparking lots of research interest.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.020
Computer modeling studies
have suggested that

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.060
certain hibiscus compounds
might bind

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.300
to the fat-digesting enzyme
lipase like a lock-and-key.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.900
Test tube studies screening
a variety of medicinal plants

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.360
did indeed find hibiscus
inhibited lipase

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.740
more than most of the others,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:33.360
and hibiscus has been found
to reduce body fat in hamsters,

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.300
mice, and rats,
increasing fecal fat excretion.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:45.000
But it wasn't tested in people
until this study published in 2014.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.760
The title gives the findings away.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.560
Spoiler alert: Hibiscus can inhibit
obesity and fat accumulation --

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.520
in humans -- and improve fatty liver.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.800
To create a randomized
double-blind trial,

00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.580
instead of trying to create

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.920
some artificially colored
and flavored placebo tea,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.520
they just dried the hibiscus tea
into powder and put it into capsules.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.060
After 12 weeks, there was
a greater reduction in waistlines

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.100
and percent body fat
in the hibiscus group,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.380
compared to those who
got placebo capsules.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.380
But the dose they ended up using
was equivalent

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.900
of like nine cups
of hibiscus tea a day.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.080
I recommend people stick
to no more than a quart a day

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.720
on a regular basis due to
the high manganese content.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.120
Manganese is an
essential trace mineral,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.020
but nine cups a day might result
in too much of a good thing.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.640
Finally, in 2018, this study was
published using a reasonable dose --

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.600
the equivalent of about a single
12-ounce glass of hibiscus tea a day.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.280
The complicating factor is that they
also added lemon verbena to the mix.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.340
That's another herbal tea, better
known for improving recovery

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.380
after intense bouts
of strength training,

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.560
but there was some promising
in vitro data on effects

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.560
of lemon verbena
on fat cells in a petri dish,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.060
so they tried a combination.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.240
It comes out to be about
a cup and a half of hibiscus tea

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.960
and a quarter cup of lemon verbena
tea once a day for two months.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.480
Both the tea and placebo
groups were fed diets

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.420
containing the same amount
of calories, yet those randomized

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.300
to the tea group lost
significantly more weight --

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.040
five pounds compared
to three pounds.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.960
That's only an extra
pound or two a month,

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.480
but an extra pound a month
eating the same number of calories.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.300
That's the advantage of
fat-blocking interventions

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.340
that actually cause you
to lose more calories

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.460
beyond just reducing hunger
and making you feel fuller longer

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.460
in hopes you'll eat fewer
calories in the first place.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.280
Why not just pop pills
instead of brewing tea?

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.060
There's all sorts of herbal extract
supplements on the market,

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.760
but that presumes we know
enough to extract out

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.380
the right active ingredients.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.040
For example, it does not appear
to be the red anthocyanin pigments

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.280
in hibiscus, since white varieties
seem to have similar effects.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.760
When the various compounds
in hibiscus tea are isolated out

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.600
and tested in various combinations,
synergistic effects are found,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.020
meaning the whole may be
greater than the sum of its parts.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:02.280
As with any sour food or beverage,
though (like after eating citrus),

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.340
it's important to wash the
natural acids off your teeth

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.760
by rinsing your mouth out with
water to protect your tooth enamel.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.480
You also want to wait
at least an hour before brushing,

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.429
so as not to erode your enamel
when it's in a softened state.

